  "notes": "Built from the 2024-25 bulletin's Suggested Academic Plan. Total credits: 126 per bulletin (original printed 123cr, +3cr for added MATH 21 prereq fix). MATH 21 added to First Year Spring matching 2026's prereq fix -- ACCTG 211/SCM 200/STAT 200 (Second Year Fall) real-require MATH 21 per the shared catalogs, never listed in Behrend's own 2024 suggested plan. Very similar to 2023 curriculum with one change: Fourth Year Fall focus-area slot reduced from 4cr to 3cr. CAS 100 marked as generic_slot per scraper. QUALITY-AUDIT FIX (2026-09-18): self-verification (build_full_plan) originally failed with 'Could not schedule' for MIS 430, MGMT 410, MIS 445, MIS 495, MGMT 471W -- all real 400-level courses gated by Faculty Senate Policy 34-00's 5th-semester registration-priority rule (standing_gate_ok), which computes standing from REAL completed-course credits only. This plan's 'General Education Course (GH/GN/GHW/GA/Inter-Domain)' slots named a domain in their own label text but never carried the machine-readable 'gen_ed' key those domains need to resolve to a real course in the simulator, so they contributed 0 credits toward standing and permanently blocked every 400-level course. Root-caused by comparing against MISBH-2026.json, whose equivalent slots all carry real 'gen_ed' keys. Added the missing 'gen_ed' key to every slot naming one single, unambiguous domain (GH, GN, GHW, GA, Inter-Domain -> INTER-D), matching 2026's exact tagging; left the two genuinely multi-domain slots untagged, same as 2026. Self-verification now passes with 0 warnings.",
